The Constitution is amended by deleting section 15 and Amendment 'or substituting therefor the following -section 4. "The Council. 15. (1) The Council shall consist of :

(a) a Chairman who shall be appointed by His Majesty The Sultan and Yang Di-Pertuan;

(b) a Deputy Chairman who shall be appointed by His Majesty The Sultan and Yang Di-Pertuan ;

(c) the Vice-Chancellor ;

(d) the Mufti of Brunei Darussalam ;

(e) not more than five (5) persons appointed by His Majesty The Sultan and Yang Di-Pertuan on the advice of the ViceChancellor ;

(f) one person elected by the Senate from among its members other than the ViceChancellor or Deputy Vice-Chancellor ;

(g) the Permanent Secretary, Ministry of Finance (or his representative) ;

(h) the Permanent Secretary, Miltistry of Education (or his representative) ;

(i) the Permanent Secretaries of such other Ministries (or their representatives) as His Majesty The Sultan and Yang Di-Pertuan may appoint, after consultation with the Chairman of the Council ; Ul the Attorney-General (or his representative) ;

(k) the Director of Establishment (or his representative) ; and

(1) one representative of the Guild of Graduates of Universiti Brunei Darussalam elected from among its members provided that such representative is not a full-time staff member of the University.

(2) The Registrar and Secretary shall be Secretary to the Council.

(3) The Deputy Chairman shall act as Chairman of the Council in the absence of the Chairman.

(4) In the absence of both the Chairman and the Deputy Chairman at any meeting of the Council, a member of the Council elected by the members present at the meeting shall preside at the meeting.

(5) Except as may be otherwise prescribed by His Majesty, the term of office of the Chairman, the Deputy Chairman and the members of the Council appointed under paragraph (e) and (i) of sub-section (1) shall be three years, calculated from the date of their appointment.

(6) The term of office of the members of the Council elected under paragraph (f) and (1) of subsection (1) shall be two years, calculated from the date of their election.

(7) A Deputy Vice-Chancellor may attend meetings of the Council but shall have no v~te." Amendment of 5. Sub-section (2) of section 17 of the Constitution is deleted and the section 17. following substituted therefor - "(2) The Vice-Chancellor may appoint a Deputy Vice-Chancellor or, if no Deputy Vice-Chancellor has been appointed, any member of the Senate to deputies for him as Chairman at any meeting of the Senate if the Vice-Chancellor is unable to attend the meeting."
